\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16.1}{\ignorespaces Support shape of every lake in the survey, coloured by verdict: green \textsc  {filled}, amber \textsc  {tail-inflated}, red \textsc  {spiked}. Only pulsar spin frequency (top right) is honest single-population support. The stitched ``universal'' composites are all spiked or tail-inflated --- the visual signature of cross-population assembly that the cross-scale-stack chapter warns is not a single lake. Nuclear half-life (\texttt  {L\_q5\_decay}) shows its characteristic single lump with an isolated placeholder spike near $\ln x \approx 58$. This one panel is the census result made visible: no honest lake resolves and locks a register.}}{49}{figure.16.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:support-shapes}{{16.1}{49}{Support shape of every lake in the survey, coloured by verdict: green \textsc {filled}, amber \textsc {tail-inflated}, red \textsc {spiked}. Only pulsar spin frequency (top right) is honest single-population support. The stitched ``universal'' composites are all spiked or tail-inflated --- the visual signature of cross-population assembly that the cross-scale-stack chapter warns is not a single lake. Nuclear half-life (\texttt {L\_q5\_decay}) shows its characteristic single lump with an isolated placeholder spike near $\ln x \approx 58$. This one panel is the census result made visible: no honest lake resolves and locks a register}{figure.16.1}{}}
